CORE broken-smt-backend broken-cprover-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--trace --beautify
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^  x=\d+ \([0 ]*1[0 ]*\)$
^  y=\d+ \([0 ]*1[0 ]*\)$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
--beautify minimises the number of bits set in the values of the counterexample:
a single bit suffices for each of x and y.
